  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why is my Legacy Piece code not working?",
      "a": "Almost every code ends in two exclamation marks, and missing one makes it fail. Also make sure your inventory is not full, since rewards can fail to arrive when it is."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does CCU mean in codes like thanksfor17kccu!!?",
      "a": "CCU stands for concurrent users, which is how many people are playing at the same time. The developers release a thank-you code each time the game reaches a new player count."
    },
    {
      "q": "Where is the code box in Legacy Piece?",
      "a": "It is inside Settings, which you open with the gear icon on the left side of the screen after pressing Play."
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Bosses give the best drops. Once you can beat one without trouble, farm it for a while before moving on to the next island.",
    "Clans, traits and abilities all shape your build. Look at what each one boosts before spending rerolls, so you know which results are worth keeping.",
    "Skill Tree Resets let you rebuild your skills from scratch. Try a few setups early, and keep one reset spare in case an update changes the balance.",
    "With a cap of 12,000, reaching max level is a very long grind. Set smaller goals like the next island or the next boss so you always have something close to aim for."
  ],
  "useRewards": "Redeem every active code, since together they give a big pile of Shards and chests. Drink a Drop Potion right before you spend Boss Tickets, so the potion is active during your boss fights. Keep Skill Tree Resets until you want to change your build. Open Ultimate Chests and Secret Gem Chests in batches and check what you got. The Cash and Aura Crates from codes like ichigospawner!! are a nice early boost.",
